step-2c72979c-0908-5fbd-85a9-ea945295a125" "step-3d43bf3e-2fb8-5456-b231-9a491908f785"] :activity/first-step "step-85a99d67-08c7-5c39-919b-70a7c169d796" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-85a99d67-08c7-5c39-919b-70a7c169d796" :step/id #uuid "85a99d67-08c7-5c39-919b-70a7c169d796" :step/content 17592186329710 :step/next "step-127f1300-1391-54f6-9fe2-9e7626e9b022" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-127f1300-1391-54f6-9fe2-9e7626e9b022" :step/id #uuid "127f1300-1391-54f6-9fe2-9e7626e9b022" :step/content 17592186120458 :step/next "step-eda35098-d403-5441-92fc-05e024fcafb1" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eda35098-d403-5441-92fc-05e024fcafb1" :step/id #uuid "eda35098-d403-5441-92fc-05e024fcafb1" :step/content 17592186416303 :step/next "step-2c72979c-0908-5fbd-85a9-ea945295a125" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2c72979c-0908-5fbd-85a9-ea945295a125" :step/id #uuid "2c72979c-0908-5fbd-85a9-ea945295a125" :step/content 17592186271995 :step/next "step-3d43bf3e-2fb8-5456-b231-9a491908f785" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-3d43bf3e-2fb8-5456-b231-9a491908f785" :step/id #uuid "3d43bf3e-2fb8-5456-b231-9a491908f785" :step/content 17592186272007 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152241 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eabcc9c8-1fae-5b8f-9d65-4f29f12ab5ce" "question-528c6dbc-6dbe-5499-88b0-b6881a756455"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eabcc9c8-1fae-5b8f-9d65-4f29f12ab5ce" :question/id #uuid "eabcc9c8-1fae-5b8f-9d65-4f29f12ab5ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-51883" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa895816cc537fc2ccb30f99f2f9c8ec01cf0ee75ba76fc8a2aed1c0b3349206.png)\n\nThe graph above shows that the volume of gas $L$ in a truck's tank is directly proportional to the time $t$ since the driver started filling it. Find a direct variation equation that describes the relationship between $L$ and $t.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $L$ varies directly with $t,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\nL=kt.\n$$\n\nNext, we notice that there is a point on the graph with $t=6$ and $L=90.$ So, we substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}90 & =k\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{90}{6} & =k \\\\ 15 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the direct variation equation is given by\n\n$$\nL=15t.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bf78e6b5-1138-5983-a5e7-632caf3ecb6f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bf78e6b5-1138-5983-a5e7-632caf3ecb6f" :answer-field/id #uuid "bf78e6b5-1138-5983-a5e7-632caf3ecb6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ea1c18ae-83f8-5cdc-a1af-f2cbf0066c61" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ea1c18ae-83f8-5cdc-a1af-f2cbf0066c61" "answer-b3983d19-ed17-57aa-997b-ec527346494e" "answer-1746c645-2ca1-5886-a22d-da171cd15a01" "answer-4e190a43-d3de-5ac0-b00b-dc513b13624d" "answer-56acae82-639f-5413-88a9-a7b04e1a0938"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea1c18ae-83f8-5cdc-a1af-f2cbf0066c61" :answer/id #uuid "ea1c18ae-83f8-5cdc-a1af-f2cbf0066c61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "L=15t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3983d19-ed17-57aa-997b-ec527346494e" :answer/id #uuid "b3983d19-ed17-57aa-997b-ec527346494e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "L=30t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1746c645-2ca1-5886-a22d-da171cd15a01" :answer/id #uuid "1746c645-2ca1-5886-a22d-da171cd15a01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "L=50t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e190a43-d3de-5ac0-b00b-dc513b13624d" :answer/id #uuid "4e190a43-d3de-5ac0-b00b-dc513b13624d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "L=60t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56acae82-639f-5413-88a9-a7b04e1a0938" :answer/id #uuid "56acae82-639f-5413-88a9-a7b04e1a0938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "L=90t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152111 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d9eeaf2b-c92c-529e-9218-24a01a5754ee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d9eeaf2b-c92c-529e-9218-24a01a5754ee" :question/id #uuid "d9eeaf2b-c92c-529e-9218-24a01a5754ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-68193" :question/problem "![](images/25/2501f7e346abf6c79a211fd090162be685c001bc6acc68787d8c73c0eee7a8af.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a proportional relationship between the weight $x$ (in pounds) of ice cream sold by a store and the profit $y$ (in dollars).  What is the constant of proportionality?" :question/worked-solution "To compute the constant of proportionality, we first need to choose a point $(x,y)$ on the graph. Here, let's choose the point $(3,4).$\n\n![](images/7b/7beacc5836ed16a4dcb36916d0273513b7b2d94871c4ee5994d56479bc11f18d.png)\n\nNow, we can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-coordinate to the $x$-coordinate, as follows:\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{y}{x}=\\frac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{3}=1\\,\\text{R}1=1\\,\\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the constant of proportionality is $1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ dollars per pound." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4c911119-b189-59c9-afe1-208ee09fedb8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c911119-b189-59c9-afe1-208ee09fedb8" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c911119-b189-59c9-afe1-208ee09fedb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b7818b8-beef-5b29-af60-15faef7c0a86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3b7818b8-beef-5b29-af60-15faef7c0a86" "answer-2f1efd6d-9c98-5e26-81d8-cffc494aafcf" "answer-9d0d083c-0799-5884-af03-185f6861a496" "answer-1d37e1bb-efc8-5170-a04c-6bd70009b86b" "answer-4b0a3f95-e65f-5423-819f-da1d3c12223c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b7818b8-beef-5b29-af60-15faef7c0a86" :answer/id #uuid "3b7818b8-beef-5b29-af60-15faef7c0a86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ dollars per pound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f1efd6d-9c98-5e26-81d8-cffc494aafcf" :answer/id #uuid "2f1efd6d-9c98-5e26-81d8-cffc494aafcf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1\\,\\frac{2}{3}$ dollars per pound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d0d083c-0799-5884-af03-185f6861a496" :answer/id #uuid "9d0d083c-0799-5884-af03-185f6861a496" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$ dollars per pound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d37e1bb-efc8-5170-a04c-6bd70009b86b" :answer/id #uuid "1d37e1bb-efc8-5170-a04c-6bd70009b86b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2\\,\\frac{1}{3}$ dollars per pound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b0a3f95-e65f-5423-819f-da1d3c12223c" :answer/id #uuid "4b0a3f95-e65f-5423-819f-da1d3c12223c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\frac{2}{3}$ dollars per pound" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-528c6dbc-6dbe-5499-88b0-b6881a756455" :question/id #uuid "528c6dbc-6dbe-5499-88b0-b6881a756455" :question/math-academy-id "q-115639" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e3a9bc6a2c642697cfa2b6525e3abf42a0227f0ac66eecade156a842fb5e92d.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a direct variation between the variables $u$ and $z.$ Which equation describes the relationship between the variables?" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ varies directly with $z,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\nu=kz.\n$$\n\nNext, we notice there is a point on the graph with $z=-10$ and $u=2.$ So, we substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =k\\cdot (-10) \\\\ -\\frac{2}{10} & =k \\\\ -\\frac{1}{5} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the direct variation equation is given by\n\n$$\nu=-\\frac{1}{5}z.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35a7e094-9492-556b-b055-0b4284ba502d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35a7e094-9492-556b-b055-0b4284ba502d" :answer-field/id #uuid "35a7e094-9492-556b-b055-0b4284ba502d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c2fd7900-c51f-5bed-9b31-6871651fb51e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-81b9413e-71d2-55bc-b120-48cf7418e25a" "answer-1a10968a-1243-571b-a9bd-8c6631c847bb" "answer-c2fd7900-c51f-5bed-9b31-6871651fb51e" "answer-bbcec67a-21f7-515b-b67b-d4dfa9b9a0fe" "answer-440df762-731d-56df-bc2f-7e0b6dfe87dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81b9413e-71d2-55bc-b120-48cf7418e25a" :answer/id #uuid "81b9413e-71d2-55bc-b120-48cf7418e25a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=-5z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1a10968a-1243-571b-a9bd-8c6631c847bb" :answer/id #uuid "1a10968a-1243-571b-a9bd-8c6631c847bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=-\\frac{1}{2}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c2fd7900-c51f-5bed-9b31-6871651fb51e" :answer/id #uuid "c2fd7900-c51f-5bed-9b31-6871651fb51e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=-\\frac{1}{5}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bbcec67a-21f7-515b-b67b-d4dfa9b9a0fe" :answer/id #uuid "bbcec67a-21f7-515b-b67b-d4dfa9b9a0fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=5z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-440df762-731d-56df-bc2f-7e0b6dfe87dd" :answer/id #uuid "440df762-731d-56df-bc2f-7e0b6dfe87dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "u=\\frac{1}{5}z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f24b3b44-c729-5176-9a67-9bc09288acd6" :activity/id #uuid "f24b3b44-c729-5176-9a67-9bc09288acd6" :activity/title "Understanding Proportional Relationships Using Graphs" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048993 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-7d66a73b-7d01-5490-b561-23c518b44d9a" "step-36a5066a-12cf-5071-9d56-323a5a484789" "step-35310a5a-f14e-5220-a85f-b4ffe8767295"] :activity/first-step "step-7d66a73b-7d01-5490-b561-23c518b44d9a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-7d66a73b-7d01-5490-b561-23c518b44d9a" :step/id #uuid "7d66a73b-7d01-5490-b561-23c518b44d9a" :step/content "question-eabcc9c8-1fae-5b8f-9d65-4f29f12ab5ce" :step/next "step-36a5066a-12cf-5071-9d56-323a5a484789" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-36a5066a-12cf-5071-9d56-323a5a484789" :step/id #uuid "36a5066a-12cf-5071-9d56-323a5a484789" :step/content "question-d9eeaf2b-c92c-529e-9218-24a01a5754ee" :step/next "step-35310a5a-f14e-5220-a85f-b4ffe8767295" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-35310a5a-f14e-5220-a85f-b4ffe8767295" :step/id #uuid "35310a5a-f14e-5220-a85f-b4ffe8767295" :step/content "question-528c6dbc-6dbe-5499-88b0-b6881a756455" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096650 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-22749eae-3c2e-573a-a168-cb568838d8f3" "question-2a129def-6612-5e6f-9d02-8b4f3371bc09" "question-e8943fb5-5821-50a1-aa29-5b9a2bc234c4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-22749eae-3c2e-573a-a168-cb568838d8f3" :question/id #uuid "22749eae-3c2e-573a-a168-cb568838d8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-119896" :question/problem "![](images/21/212a339585b98f156d68f2e4260c0acbb474c51782b6d72acf0b89fd5c1fe69e.png)\n\nGiven the vectors $a$ and $b$ shown above, which of the following could be the linear combination $2a-2b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n2a-2b=2a+(-2b).\n$$\n\n- The vector $2a$ has the same direction as $a$ but twice the magnitude.\n\n- The vector $-2b$ has the direction that is opposite to $b$ but twice the magnitude.\n\n![](images/c1/c1cc845ddfe16f12169625e5f8404d3d92558b885ffde8c3ab02cdb2c096f699.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $-2b$ starting from the head of $2a.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n2a-2b\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $2a$ to the head of $-2b.$\n\n![](images/5d/5d22db7e37ff1c5b55f1ec595da919f987a6c1fea4247cf5a075f27c198ba545.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dac0f540-8539-5e56-8a7f-2c1905324354"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dac0f540-8539-5e56-8a7f-2c1905324354" :answer-field/id #uuid "dac0f540-8539-5e56-8a7f-2c1905324354" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41b2c190-c96a-5b7a-8e39-3ab87babffe3" "answer-e7600fa9-42ca-564f-81ec-880c6e921c12" "answer-3d1a9505-4a57-58e9-980d-c757aef01b68" "answer-eee8e964-460c-5f6f-8867-7d295205b3b6" "answer-b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41b2c190-c96a-5b7a-8e39-3ab87babffe3" :answer/id #uuid "41b2c190-c96a-5b7a-8e39-3ab87babffe3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/0e/0e546fdbe00f491e20354feb8dd46bf27112c464a873c3a388247a2d7dcc9de9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7600fa9-42ca-564f-81ec-880c6e921c12" :answer/id #uuid "e7600fa9-42ca-564f-81ec-880c6e921c12" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/95/950ecbf1899a038c92fe4e0b6a299de42ca1d3e897ce85b28cc94166e7e51665.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d1a9505-4a57-58e9-980d-c757aef01b68" :answer/id #uuid "3d1a9505-4a57-58e9-980d-c757aef01b68" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9d/9d2c12b802901e16ab38b37773ead31e68aa6b86b8186fa351af2af21e4d84e4.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eee8e964-460c-5f6f-8867-7d295205b3b6" :answer/id #uuid "eee8e964-460c-5f6f-8867-7d295205b3b6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cc/cca6562873f89aa7f36b13fe7e8c5646cbdbde98c8238abc99eda6d8b24ce1e9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877" :answer/id #uuid "b36a8732-0d62-56f7-b9eb-963fdbcde877" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/de/de03a1be920089723cdf3ab761a7ab02a3bbfe085ac9eb927a7dcd7163b458b1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2a129def-6612-5e6f-9d02-8b4f3371bc09" :question/id #uuid "2a129def-6612-5e6f-9d02-8b4f3371bc09" :question/math-academy-id "q-77510" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f2e79d1a16c7bba471bed8a443673449c7398486d19a84e12a91ca514c793329.png)\n\nGiven the vectors $p$ and $q$ shown above, which of the following could be the linear combination $-2p-4q?$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n-2p-4q=-2p+(-4q).\n$$\n\n- The vector $-2p$ has the direction that is opposite to $p$ and $2$ times the magnitude.\n\n- The vector $-4q$ has the direction that is opposite to $q$ and $4$ times the magnitude.\n\n![](images/de/de82fa1937ae9f7ccb1b739cc8e6ea9848a71ea216df600917706717711aa081.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $-4q$ starting from the head of $-2p.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n-2p-4q\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $-2p$ to the head of $-4q.$\n\n![](images/2d/2d388be7761bd2fbae0593b8e715f1873e4170e577132b4a6838412e3629c480.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9a543759-f32b-5fef-8ec7-75450be60a35"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9a543759-f32b-5fef-8ec7-75450be60a35" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a543759-f32b-5fef-8ec7-75450be60a35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19518956-bd5f-5186-bc80-a603a1eda7da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e9240848-683b-5515-aa41-d623e851288f" "answer-19518956-bd5f-5186-bc80-a603a1eda7da" "answer-112d6e45-f7c7-5fd0-9c28-59f156bc4fb4" "answer-1fd898bc-282c-5bec-bd5a-748eaff375ea" "answer-573d27c8-86a5-57a8-899b-5ba8a595d566"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e9240848-683b-5515-aa41-d623e851288f" :answer/id #uuid "e9240848-683b-5515-aa41-d623e851288f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/41/4146c89c85502a011c98ef41f7744717286840606161bb3101dd462ea9f736ce.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19518956-bd5f-5186-bc80-a603a1eda7da" :answer/id #uuid "19518956-bd5f-5186-bc80-a603a1eda7da" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9a/9a455b1d56f155619470063a5d08751b3a5baf19e3ecee6086397f9ff7498649.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-112d6e45-f7c7-5fd0-9c28-59f156bc4fb4" :answer/id #uuid "112d6e45-f7c7-5fd0-9c28-59f156bc4fb4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/9e/9ed635e991a7b8243cc125083e5f4a3d2a8dc805dde41c3518f78556d690bd11.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fd898bc-282c-5bec-bd5a-748eaff375ea" :answer/id #uuid "1fd898bc-282c-5bec-bd5a-748eaff375ea" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ae/ae9531d13b148e7dd23ce1a06506902dfede35e39d826bdd47cfa540dd31f80f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-573d27c8-86a5-57a8-899b-5ba8a595d566" :answer/id #uuid "573d27c8-86a5-57a8-899b-5ba8a595d566" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f3/f36333620d7da91c4b11c5773f7948c6946a3fcb8cd6192f4b873f9b1e39e437.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8943fb5-5821-50a1-aa29-5b9a2bc234c4" :question/id #uuid "e8943fb5-5821-50a1-aa29-5b9a2bc234c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-77509" :question/problem "![](images/66/667454b0cdd06afe7b722aad8ad64423491e8e13a3eb950945af7bedcb7291c9.png)\n\nGiven the vectors $a$ and $b$ shown above, which of the following could be the linear combination $-4a-3b?$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall that\n\n$$\n-4a-3b=-4a+(-3b).\n$$\n\n- The vector $-4a$ has the direction that is opposite to $a$ and $4$ times the magnitude.\n\n- The vector $-b$ has the direction that is opposite to $b$ and $3$ times the magnitude.\n\n![](images/fb/fb02d818d2ad88acc13802287bc02fa194afba38ec018429b867fe5f21a6206e.png)\n\nNow, we can draw $-3b$ starting from the head of $-4a.$ The resultant \n\n$$\n-4a-3b\n$$\n\ngoes from the tail of $-4a$ to the head of $-3b.$\n\n![](images/e3/e30a16feb7f1fcc75789443db72de1fda10b61762401d19ee296df11aa03b09d.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9eda16f6-069f-5f9f-8e85-00b3cc377912"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9eda16f6-069f-5f9f-8e85-00b3cc377912" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda16f6-069f-5f9f-8e85-00b3cc377912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" "answer-0e0ff1ca-08d1-5d11-a958-2853ad1d3478" "answer-1e013e1c-7c1c-5b98-8dc9-2b995e4ac6c5" "answer-ab0a2627-b32a-5580-9b78-033d4b2da069" "answer-141e56de-8f45-541d-80e5-6168d1b1af22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" :answer/id #uuid "dba9332c-d2ae-5f67-be78-45a6264c9e39" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1e/1e1de76cd9d9a36b31aa086d5373cd5e6d11c876fd47c683058e6a6741b641b1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e0ff1ca-08d1-5d11-a958-2853ad1d3478" :answer/id #uuid "0e0ff1ca-08d1-5d11-a958-2853ad1d3478" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/4c/4c623b59994ea799279ddb9f878a4418d8885cf789a0f0fbae3f920b76dc98d6.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e013e1c-7c1c-5b98-8dc9-2b995e4ac6c5" :answer/id #uuid "1e013e1c-7c1c-5b98-8dc9-2b995e4ac6c5" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/c2/c2a173ea1937ac228c9f69bcba2b0f2d04cf5ad018b64912b7ba397ff9a3c068.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab0a2627-b32a-5580-9b78-033d4b2da069" :answer/id #uuid "ab0a2627-b32a-5580-9b78-033d4b2da069" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/d9/d9be31d60b73be662c7dfe957e932a5fcd8c37c78cb4a75551047607e65081cd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-141e56de-8f45-541d-80e5-6168d1b1af22" :answer/id #uuid "141e56de-8f45-541d-80e5-6168d1b1af22" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ff/ffa6ea463246b87bdbc767111d72805015ad3b40895696b54051c31a8785e30c.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096651 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d2a5cac6-33f2-5ce9-8655-67db2ef94b7e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d2a5cac6-33f2-5ce9-8655-67db2ef94b7e" :question/id #uuid "d2a5cac6-33f2-5ce9-8655-67db2ef94b7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-277079" :question/problem "Suppose we are given two vectors $a$ and $b$ where $a∦b.$ Find $\\lambda$ and $\\mu ,$ if \n\n$$\na-2b=(3\\lambda -\\mu )a-(\\lambda -4\\mu )b.\n$$\n\n$\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,\\mu =$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "Since $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. So, the coefficients of $a$ must be equal, and the coefficients of $b$ must be equal.\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3\\lambda -\\mu &=1 \\\\ \\lambda -4\\mu &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\mu =3\\lambda -1\n$$\n\nSubstituting back into the second equation, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda -4\\mu  & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -4(3\\lambda -1) & =2 \\\\ \\lambda -12\\lambda +4 & =2 \\\\ -11\\lambda  & =-2 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\frac{2}{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =3\\lambda -1 \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{11}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c60f15ed-8ce7-5564-85f4-7485ed35b513" "answer-field-ab223a15-b693-5906-bf6e-72560257b340"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c60f15ed-8ce7-5564-85f4-7485ed35b513" :answer-field/id #uuid "c60f15ed-8ce7-5564-85f4-7485ed35b513" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34" :answer-field/choices ["answer-915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34" :answer/id #uuid "915b5a1a-8b66-53b2-a236-d722c0a8dc34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ab223a15-b693-5906-bf6e-72560257b340" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab223a15-b693-5906-bf6e-72560257b340" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5" :answer/id #uuid "1c02f9d2-6489-5d8d-80e2-8043d16c70c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096970 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097835 :tutorial/content "A **linear combination** of two vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is a sum of multiples of the two vectors. \n\nFor example, let's consider the vectors $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b,$ shown below:\n\n![](images/00/0091edb7bcd026737e7bdf9d56e5a9932970d62902a185f76599cdf18bfd9d45.png)\n\nOne particular linear combination of these vectors is \n\n$$\n2 \\mathbf{a} + 3 \\mathbf{b} = 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{a} + 3 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nIf we draw this linear combination in the coordinate plane, we get the following:\n\n![](images/73/73a73b7e90c9e82e57f88d04079a69fa2cce082fc6d7f4667fae1cb4190ea46a.png)" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097836 :tutorial/content "If two vectors are not parallel, then each linear combination can only be written in one way. \n\nFor example, if we have two vectors $\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{b}$ with $\\mathbf{a} \\nparallel \\mathbf{b},$ and two real numbers $\\alpha,\\beta,$ then the equality\n\n$$\n2 \\mathbf{a} + 3 \\mathbf{b} = \\alpha \\mathbf{a} + \\beta \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nholds if and only if $\\alpha=2$ and $\\beta=3$.\n\nIn other words, the pair of numbers $\\alpha,\\beta$ defines a unique vector $\\alpha \\mathbf{a} + \\beta \\mathbf{b}.$ That is to say, if\n\n$$\n\\alpha_1 \\mathbf{a} + \\beta_1 \\mathbf{b} = \\alpha_2 \\mathbf{a} + \\beta_2 \\mathbf{b},\n$$\n\nthen $\\alpha_1 = \\alpha_2$ and $\\beta_1 = \\beta_2.$\n\n**Watch out!** This property holds only if two vectors *are not parallel*." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096885 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7fe1aa9d-37dc-5179-a9aa-2b200892c342"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7fe1aa9d-37dc-5179-a9aa-2b200892c342" :question/id #uuid "7fe1aa9d-37dc-5179-a9aa-2b200892c342" :question/math-academy-id "q-42470" :question/problem "Find $6det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6det(A)-2det(B)=6\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-115943c0-4406-5318-97d2-aaaf6a81b1a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-115943c0-4406-5318-97d2-aaaf6a81b1a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "115943c0-4406-5318-97d2-aaaf6a81b1a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09" :answer-field/choices ["answer-eb75d285-a0d6-5f8c-a9c2-836a45c2758a" "answer-be14d03c-9132-5936-8238-efc2e8f7723f" "answer-20634a88-ab85-5824-bb75-747bedffe291" "answer-8d3dde88-c021-53a6-a9b7-fc728d6e08ce" "answer-1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb75d285-a0d6-5f8c-a9c2-836a45c2758a" :answer/id #uuid "eb75d285-a0d6-5f8c-a9c2-836a45c2758a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be14d03c-9132-5936-8238-efc2e8f7723f" :answer/id #uuid "be14d03c-9132-5936-8238-efc2e8f7723f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20634a88-ab85-5824-bb75-747bedffe291" :answer/id #uuid "20634a88-ab85-5824-bb75-747bedffe291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d3dde88-c021-53a6-a9b7-fc728d6e08ce" :answer/id #uuid "8d3dde88-c021-53a6-a9b7-fc728d6e08ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09" :answer/id #uuid "1edf89ea-e738-5eda-a1d9-edeb56378f09" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133913 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3e928130-63ab-538e-924b-5fd72d363a24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e928130-63ab-538e-924b-5fd72d363a24" :question/id #uuid "3e928130-63ab-538e-924b-5fd72d363a24" :question/math-academy-id "q-42880" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has proportional columns\n\nIII. $A$ has identical rows" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional rows: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have proportional columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76065098-0f94-561f-87a2-0208d448f13f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76065098-0f94-561f-87a2-0208d448f13f" :answer-field/id #uuid "76065098-0f94-561f-87a2-0208d448f13f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25e65798-8cb9-5e6a-90b2-bc96c42a9ab2" "answer-4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" "answer-ef8c45cd-d498-500f-8405-f10838f41de4" "answer-dc571830-aa37-5965-b6b0-fb4b6669513b" "answer-ab29bb3a-73e2-5e1e-8a70-ef9505fc697d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25e65798-8cb9-5e6a-90b2-bc96c42a9ab2" :answer/id #uuid "25e65798-8cb9-5e6a-90b2-bc96c42a9ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" :answer/id #uuid "4ee883f2-99ad-5639-b372-bda98b47efa9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef8c45cd-d498-500f-8405-f10838f41de4" :answer/id #uuid "ef8c45cd-d498-500f-8405-f10838f41de4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc571830-aa37-5965-b6b0-fb4b6669513b" :answer/id #uuid "dc571830-aa37-5965-b6b0-fb4b6669513b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab29bb3a-73e2-5e1e-8a70-ef9505fc697d" :answer/id #uuid "ab29bb3a-73e2-5e1e-8a70-ef9505fc697d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135151 :tutorial/content "If an $n\\!\\times \\!n$ matrix $A$ has an entire row or column of zeros, then its determinant is equal to zero.\n\nFor example, consider the matrix $A$ given below:\n\n![](images/6b/6bb8b64f7ed8730e641cdf88fc6fe7add40bc15061095c6b1f57c1b764b28feb.svg)\n\nThe second row consists of all zeros, and the asterisks ($\\ast$) may represent any number.\n\nLet's compute the determinant using the Laplace expansion across the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2+1}(0)\\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)^{2+2}(0)\\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{vmatrix}+(-1)^{2+3}(0)\\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0+0+0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that it doesn't matter what numbers are represented by the asterisks ($\\ast$). Each cofactor is multiplied by zero, so the final result must be zero." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129146 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0d6ccda5-f064-5d51-bbf4-385a52f598a9" "question-bec25d7a-3c2c-5bfa-ad41-b6aabdf70b0c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0d6ccda5-f064-5d51-bbf4-385a52f598a9" :question/id #uuid "0d6ccda5-f064-5d51-bbf4-385a52f598a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-28194" :question/problem "Given that $(x+1)$ is a factor of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-4x-2,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to factor the polynomial. We are told that $(x+1)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so $(x+1)$ divides $f(x)$ with zero remainder. To begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x+1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & -1 & -3 & -4 & -2 \\\\  &  & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\  & -1 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(x)}{x+1} & =-{x}^{2}-2x-2 \\\\  & =-({x}^{2}+2x+2),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nf(x)=-(x+1)({x}^{2}+2x+2).\n$$\n\nThe equation is now fully factored. Note that the discriminant of ${x}^{2}+2x+2=0$ is \n\n$$\nD={2}^{2}-4(1)(2)=-4<0,\n$$\n\nwhich implies that the quadratic factor has no real roots. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that $f(x)$ has a single root at $x=-1.$ \n\nWe also find the $y$-intercept of the curve by substituting the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\ny=-(0)^{3}-3(0)^{2}-4(0)-2=-2\n$$\n\nSo, the curve:\n\n- has a $y$-intercept at $(0,-2),$\n\n- passes through the $x$-axis at the single root $x=-1,$ and\n\n- has no more $x$-intercepts.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the graph has an $\\text{S}$-shape. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/de/de0741fcb960e2b140660ac01307c8d6e69c3998fb79233ba8d17755c3d10fc0.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b3431335-323c-5343-839e-0e15fdbf3890"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b3431335-323c-5343-839e-0e15fdbf3890" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3431335-323c-5343-839e-0e15fdbf3890" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf099139-689e-5f75-a4dd-b68446c6bcde" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc99f072-396e-58d8-abba-10c6fdf37ceb" "answer-57886281-56d8-54cd-b5ee-42e3787e64c6" "answer-a9bb3a61-8a73-5f70-964d-bf48a4acfd84" "answer-f2efe1eb-3bf2-5ed9-a383-1cd9053f65ea" "answer-cf099139-689e-5f75-a4dd-b68446c6bcde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc99f072-396e-58d8-abba-10c6fdf37ceb" :answer/id #uuid "cc99f072-396e-58d8-abba-10c6fdf37ceb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/29/296e6670d8c9eff997f6f6f4e186e4b0219177cfa860a64a2b257cbc1e81c216.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57886281-56d8-54cd-b5ee-42e3787e64c6" :answer/id #uuid "57886281-56d8-54cd-b5ee-42e3787e64c6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b6/b648cf07daf5babeb4bcfc064a09e5ad18c72f1f8811121dc7a57ab6dd31b47a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9bb3a61-8a73-5f70-964d-bf48a4acfd84" :answer/id #uuid "a9bb3a61-8a73-5f70-964d-bf48a4acfd84" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ce/cebfee355cc0ea19dbfe16a949269070792aa2b017637a78440f1c86d3c93e96.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f2efe1eb-3bf2-5ed9-a383-1cd9053f65ea" :answer/id #uuid "f2efe1eb-3bf2-5ed9-a383-1cd9053f65ea" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/cf/cf4acc2efcee2c592809e993cdf68c937396320b42122fd8eeb5deb83b6c2619.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf099139-689e-5f75-a4dd-b68446c6bcde" :answer/id #uuid "cf099139-689e-5f75-a4dd-b68446c6bcde" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/de/de0741fcb960e2b140660ac01307c8d6e69c3998fb79233ba8d17755c3d10fc0.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129141 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-88a63990-6594-5760-b73c-c8f3ff85a424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-88a63990-6594-5760-b73c-c8f3ff85a424" :question/id #uuid "88a63990-6594-5760-b73c-c8f3ff85a424" :question/math-academy-id "q-38949" :question/problem "Given that $(x+1)$ is a factor of $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+3x+3,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to factor the polynomial. We are told that $(x+1)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so $(x+1)$ divides $f(x)$ with zero remainder. To begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x+1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\  &  & -1 & 0 & -3 \\\\  & 1 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{f(x)}{x+1}={x}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+1)({x}^{2}+3).\n$$\n\nThe equation is now fully factored. Note that the discriminant of ${x}^{2}+3=0$ is \n\n$$\nD={0}^{2}-4(1)(3)=-12<0,\n$$\n\nwhich implies that the quadratic factor has no real roots. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that $f(x)$ has a single root at $x=-1.$ \n\nWe also find the $y$-intercept of the curve by substituting the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={0}^{3}+{0}^{2}+3(0)+3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the curve:\n\n- has a $y$-intercept at $(0,3),$\n\n- passes through the $x$-axis at the single root $x=-1,$ and\n\n- has no more $x$-intercepts.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the graph takes an inverted $\\text{S}$-shape. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/6f/6f9f2ce252975ee7c375071a74256b1e3a8822fbea8c2787af20f566a495102a.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13d53b8e-b395-5585-a8ae-f571e3f96687"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13d53b8e-b395-5585-a8ae-f571e3f96687" :answer-field/id #uuid "13d53b8e-b395-5585-a8ae-f571e3f96687" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-76bbeca7-f809-59dc-96bc-cb9ef46fa3f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9bc014c9-a389-5239-9d37-21c4b6a45e78" "answer-76bbeca7-f809-59dc-96bc-cb9ef46fa3f1" "answer-3c1d31c7-1766-52ff-801d-c1018b5cf8ec" "answer-cfec009b-afc3-58ef-9bdd-50c4ae92d4de" "answer-9c66d0b5-973e-532e-b772-7880b8902102"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bc014c9-a389-5239-9d37-21c4b6a45e78" :answer/id #uuid "9bc014c9-a389-5239-9d37-21c4b6a45e78" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/5f/5f5dbab60c5fc142d370001eac4d7f3504e988d58f41a854b497b17d9ae31a9d.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-76bbeca7-f809-59dc-96bc-cb9ef46fa3f1" :answer/id #uuid "76bbeca7-f809-59dc-96bc-cb9ef46fa3f1" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/6f/6f9f2ce252975ee7c375071a74256b1e3a8822fbea8c2787af20f566a495102a.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c1d31c7-1766-52ff-801d-c1018b5cf8ec" :answer/id #uuid "3c1d31c7-1766-52ff-801d-c1018b5cf8ec" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a7/a7fb57dc38c68d733c3d542d38c72535ba98282a15faec590ab258667969a3eb.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cfec009b-afc3-58ef-9bdd-50c4ae92d4de" :answer/id #uuid "cfec009b-afc3-58ef-9bdd-50c4ae92d4de" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ad/ad4d35c6082cd767fc770c0aaa784dd653294f3dad0361c16c31905299175912.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c66d0b5-973e-532e-b772-7880b8902102" :answer/id #uuid "9c66d0b5-973e-532e-b772-7880b8902102" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f6/f62a611bb3801a116885c625e98455768f8d2b7c14a61e6ff41e8f0c16c124e7.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-bec25d7a-3c2c-5bfa-ad41-b6aabdf70b0c" :question/id #uuid "bec25d7a-3c2c-5bfa-ad41-b6aabdf70b0c" :question/math-academy-id "q-39041" :question/problem "Given that $x$ is a factor of $f(x)=-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-4x,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" :question/worked-solution "First, let's factor the polynomial. We factor out a common factor $-x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =-{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-4x \\\\  & =-x({x}^{2}+2x+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation is now fully factored. Note that the discriminant of ${x}^{2}+2x+4=0$ is \n\n$$\nD={2}^{2}-4(1)(4)=-12<0,\n$$\n\nwhich implies that the quadratic factor has no real roots. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that $f(x)$ has a single root at $x=0.$ \n\nWe also find the $y$-intercept of the curve by substituting the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\ny=-{0}^{3}-2(0)^{2}-4(0)=0\n$$\n\nSo, the curve:\n\n- has a $y$-intercept at $(0,0),$\n\n- passes through the $x$-axis at the single root $x=0,$ and\n\n- has no more $x$-intercepts.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the graph has an $\\text{S}$-shape. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](images/f6/f621534a395f8b0692d31bb3b491b0237877e6dc3ea94a2299d354857c7c3bfd.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b6872c8f-cb1d-508e-9ef1-d93eedaf47d0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b6872c8f-cb1d-508e-9ef1-d93eedaf47d0" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6872c8f-cb1d-508e-9ef1-d93eedaf47d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a179156b-6c47-515a-b1a1-990c9e61b6d0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-22d3ed53-480e-5d14-b210-0937b5a16efb" "answer-c77677fb-023f-5df7-b72b-281a41661a3e" "answer-48acf1e2-58b9-5241-a083-38d03bb7ecb6" "answer-5ab45d73-c28c-5b3d-af71-f611454a0422" "answer-a179156b-6c47-515a-b1a1-990c9e61b6d0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22d3ed53-480e-5d14-b210-0937b5a16efb" :answer/id #uuid "22d3ed53-480e-5d14-b210-0937b5a16efb" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/0c/0ca192db022a0c468fbbf3164b8e69ca0a6c836dcbda854fa681e254534fd23f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c77677fb-023f-5df7-b72b-281a41661a3e" :answer/id #uuid "c77677fb-023f-5df7-b72b-281a41661a3e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/1b/1bc6a076bab27bb8637412fcae42e0d778b558b43c10c4654293ad0e33d54a16.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-48acf1e2-58b9-5241-a083-38d03bb7ecb6" :answer/id #uuid "48acf1e2-58b9-5241-a083-38d03bb7ecb6" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/23/235421688cb2a0f7c2d8d2720dd508ea3f9dd6f4f149b152c3bd4441c6b218f2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ab45d73-c28c-5b3d-af71-f611454a0422" :answer/id #uuid "5ab45d73-c28c-5b3d-af71-f611454a0422" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/b9/b9fbeec18a2cbaab7847c87822e1739e2759665c55b692bb4f0160285b8e1614.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a179156b-6c47-515a-b1a1-990c9e61b6d0" :answer/id #uuid "a179156b-6c47-515a-b1a1-990c9e61b6d0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/f6/f621534a395f8b0692d31bb3b491b0237877e6dc3ea94a2299d354857c7c3bfd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a69ca5e3-a84e-59d6-93a3-091c2895e2a2" :activity/id #uuid "a69ca5e3-a84e-59d6-93a3-091c2895e2a2" :activity/title "Graphing Cubic Curves Containing One Distinct Real Root" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049105 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-f38c45ec-f7e7-5e6d-bfaf-abc01579077f" "step-27e75034-4701-5c22-a371-03bed6e619ad" "step-f5acfea7-f360-5a2b-8c6f-494fe18b8b17"] :activity/first-step "step-f38c45ec-f7e7-5e6d-bfaf-abc01579077f" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f38c45ec-f7e7-5e6d-bfaf-abc01579077f" :step/id #uuid "f38c45ec-f7e7-5e6d-bfaf-abc01579077f" :step/content "question-0d6ccda5-f064-5d51-bbf4-385a52f598a9" :step/next "step-27e75034-4701-5c22-a371-03bed6e619ad" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-27e75034-4701-5c22-a371-03bed6e619ad" :step/id #uuid "27e75034-4701-5c22-a371-03bed6e619ad" :step/content "question-88a63990-6594-5760-b73c-c8f3ff85a424" :step/next "step-f5acfea7-f360-5a2b-8c6f-494fe18b8b17" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-f5acfea7-f360-5a2b-8c6f-494fe18b8b17" :step/id #uuid "f5acfea7-f360-5a2b-8c6f-494fe18b8b17" :step/content "question-bec25d7a-3c2c-5bfa-ad41-b6aabdf70b0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119938 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f8c786dd-8e95-5f38-8555-c19baa5a85a4" "question-7acf7423-e8b7-5b28-a3d4-100be04f8153"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f8c786dd-8e95-5f38-8555-c19baa5a85a4" :question/id #uuid "f8c786dd-8e95-5f38-8555-c19baa5a85a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48388" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & =\\frac{9(0)^{3}-4(0)}{3(0)^{2}+2(0)}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & =\\frac{x(9{x}^{2}-4)}{x(3x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9{x}^{2}-4}{3x+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{3}-4x}{3{x}^{2}+2x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{9{x}^{2}-4}{3x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-4}{0+2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5de46a5c-045a-5a65-93fe-1ee8641452b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5de46a5c-045a-5a65-93fe-1ee8641452b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5de46a5c-045a-5a65-93fe-1ee8641452b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f33d6f17-9ed5-585c-ab3c-2a4e63e824bc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f33d6f17-9ed5-585c-ab3c-2a4e63e824bc" "answer-b0943d78-afb5-5b99-822e-4d82efc4099b" "answer-74947654-7873-5a49-873e-6e8a7c42d1c0" "answer-3a948208-572a-5fd8-9cc1-d9a5ab2b4a9e" "answer-2daf76a0-8500-574d-afca-1701571dfa88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f33d6f17-9ed5-585c-ab3c-2a4e63e824bc" :answer/id #uuid "f33d6f17-9ed5-585c-ab3c-2a4e63e824bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0943d78-afb5-5b99-822e-4d82efc4099b" :answer/id #uuid "b0943d78-afb5-5b99-822e-4d82efc4099b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74947654-7873-5a49-873e-6e8a7c42d1c0" :answer/id #uuid "74947654-7873-5a49-873e-6e8a7c42d1c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a948208-572a-5fd8-9cc1-d9a5ab2b4a9e" :answer/id #uuid "3a948208-572a-5fd8-9cc1-d9a5ab2b4a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2daf76a0-8500-574d-afca-1701571dfa88" :answer/id #uuid "2daf76a0-8500-574d-afca-1701571dfa88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119942 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0496054d-648c-503a-af82-71aac17fd7ca"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0496054d-648c-503a-af82-71aac17fd7ca" :question/id #uuid "0496054d-648c-503a-af82-71aac17fd7ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-67981" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-3}{{x}^{2}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-3}{{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{(-1)^{2}-2(-1)-3}{(-1)^{2}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-3}{{x}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{(x+1)(x-3)}{(x-1)(x+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-3}{x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x-3}{{x}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x-3}{x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-3}{-1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4}{-2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c166c720-f30f-53d5-b633-d02350cfb530"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c166c720-f30f-53d5-b633-d02350cfb530" :answer-field/id #uuid "c166c720-f30f-53d5-b633-d02350cfb530" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dfef8bf6-a200-5160-b0c0-0fc8f8a3312c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-91881f5a-186b-5d3f-97c9-7622ea19b498" "answer-d59bae02-6f8d-59be-922b-a8707a090036" "answer-44fc1e65-39b7-53d3-8c38-1cf0053850be" "answer-dfef8bf6-a200-5160-b0c0-0fc8f8a3312c" "answer-760f0c51-eb09-5ae7-863a-50b68e94109a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-91881f5a-186b-5d3f-97c9-7622ea19b498" :answer/id #uuid "91881f5a-186b-5d3f-97c9-7622ea19b498" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d59bae02-6f8d-59be-922b-a8707a090036" :answer/id #uuid "d59bae02-6f8d-59be-922b-a8707a090036" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44fc1e65-39b7-53d3-8c38-1cf0053850be" :answer/id #uuid "44fc1e65-39b7-53d3-8c38-1cf0053850be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfef8bf6-a200-5160-b0c0-0fc8f8a3312c" :answer/id #uuid "dfef8bf6-a200-5160-b0c0-0fc8f8a3312c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-760f0c51-eb09-5ae7-863a-50b68e94109a" :answer/id #uuid "760f0c51-eb09-5ae7-863a-50b68e94109a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7acf7423-e8b7-5b28-a3d4-100be04f8153" :question/id #uuid "7acf7423-e8b7-5b28-a3d4-100be04f8153" :question/math-academy-id "q-107050" :question/problem "Evaluate ${lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6}.$" :question/worked-solution "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & =\\frac{{3}^{3}-9(3)}{{3}^{2}-5(3)+6}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & =\\frac{y({y}^{2}-9)}{(y-2)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y(y-3)(y+3)}{(y-2)(y-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{y(y+3)}{(y-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{{y}^{3}-9y}{{y}^{2}-5y+6} & ={lim}_{y\\to 3}\\frac{y(y+3)}{y-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(3+3)}{3-2} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8d7ede5a-d5a6-5e6e-9812-54ef505e6966"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8d7ede5a-d5a6-5e6e-9812-54ef505e6966" :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7ede5a-d5a6-5e6e-9812-54ef505e6966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-64ba839f-a12f-57b7-8daf-7af8a737912a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bad7f3c-66cb-5a2b-a2bb-6ac8015817b3" "answer-64ba839f-a12f-57b7-8daf-7af8a737912a" "answer-6ff234b9-3d6c-566d-84d6-2fca579d2ca0" "answer-40e6c1f3-a022-5a8d-9468-6645788684f