his reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-1}{4x-7} &=\\frac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4x-7+7-1}{4x-7} & =\\frac{4x-7}{4x-7}+\\frac{7-1}{4x-7} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{6}{4x-7}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $a=1$ and $b=6,$ and we get\n\n$$\na+b=1+6=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0b37f42c-dcbd-5572-b8fc-d3cf6928d353"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0b37f42c-dcbd-5572-b8fc-d3cf6928d353" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b37f42c-dcbd-5572-b8fc-d3cf6928d353" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0ec33733-a92b-513a-8b3a-441394690614" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8513669d-7bff-5157-b69b-9aeddb648094" "answer-aebed835-e63b-5938-9cad-6b9f4db797ef" "answer-08b9d701-17fb-509e-8c7b-01064dbfe77e" "answer-38f33d30-e38c-5faa-9338-dbf365de000d" "answer-0ec33733-a92b-513a-8b3a-441394690614"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8513669d-7bff-5157-b69b-9aeddb648094" :answer/id #uuid "8513669d-7bff-5157-b69b-9aeddb648094" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aebed835-e63b-5938-9cad-6b9f4db797ef" :answer/id #uuid "aebed835-e63b-5938-9cad-6b9f4db797ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-08b9d701-17fb-509e-8c7b-01064dbfe77e" :answer/id #uuid "08b9d701-17fb-509e-8c7b-01064dbfe77e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38f33d30-e38c-5faa-9338-dbf365de000d" :answer/id #uuid "38f33d30-e38c-5faa-9338-dbf365de000d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ec33733-a92b-513a-8b3a-441394690614" :answer/id #uuid "0ec33733-a92b-513a-8b3a-441394690614" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e60ce661-ee8f-513d-978f-4505c3b6113e" :question/id #uuid "e60ce661-ee8f-513d-978f-4505c3b6113e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319887" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{7{x}^{2}+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{7{x}^{2}-x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">$7{x}^{2}+11$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">\n{{field-2}} \n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">$7{x}^{2}-x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$7{x}^{2}-x$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\, &=\\,\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x+x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x+x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x} & =\\frac{7{x}^{2}-x}{7{x}^{2}-x}+\\frac{x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{x+11}{7{x}^{2}-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9598e78-a214-52b2-8ddf-fd78a112790d" "answer-field-530ba967-fb51-5147-9beb-a54a4c2cbcd1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9598e78-a214-52b2-8ddf-fd78a112790d" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9598e78-a214-52b2-8ddf-fd78a112790d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-04e2c946-62a1-5997-9aaa-d03ba638dfce" :answer-field/choices ["answer-04e2c946-62a1-5997-9aaa-d03ba638dfce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-04e2c946-62a1-5997-9aaa-d03ba638dfce" :answer/id #uuid "04e2c946-62a1-5997-9aaa-d03ba638dfce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-530ba967-fb51-5147-9beb-a54a4c2cbcd1" :answer-field/id #uuid "530ba967-fb51-5147-9beb-a54a4c2cbcd1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d4628792-4682-5a1d-a874-d58d1eaf6e72" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d4628792-4682-5a1d-a874-d58d1eaf6e72"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d4628792-4682-5a1d-a874-d58d1eaf6e72" :answer/id #uuid "d4628792-4682-5a1d-a874-d58d1eaf6e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2560be5d-dea1-5429-b927-2f169d6e2bc3" :question/id #uuid "2560be5d-dea1-5429-b927-2f169d6e2bc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-320734" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{3{x}^{6}+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}$ in the form $a+\\frac{bx+c}{3{x}^{6}+2x},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{6}+8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">\n{{field-2}} \n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{6}+2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"25\">$3{x}^{6}+2x$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we add and subtract $2x$ in the numerator. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{6}+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\, &=\\,\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x} & =\\frac{3{x}^{6}+2x}{3{x}^{4}+2x}+\\frac{-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{-2x+8}{3{x}^{6}+2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24b07630-8e0e-5bd4-9fd6-7d99d663bf65" "answer-field-06cc8abc-9969-520a-92ec-da121eb11e0e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24b07630-8e0e-5bd4-9fd6-7d99d663bf65" :answer-field/id #uuid "24b07630-8e0e-5bd4-9fd6-7d99d663bf65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-16245121-faf6-59e2-91c2-178909efd6ec" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16245121-faf6-59e2-91c2-178909efd6ec"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16245121-faf6-59e2-91c2-178909efd6ec" :answer/id #uuid "16245121-faf6-59e2-91c2-178909efd6ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-06cc8abc-9969-520a-92ec-da121eb11e0e" :answer-field/id #uuid "06cc8abc-9969-520a-92ec-da121eb11e0e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8d846a64-abc2-5e79-900f-14546c13193f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8d846a64-abc2-5e79-900f-14546c13193f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8d846a64-abc2-5e79-900f-14546c13193f" :answer/id #uuid "8d846a64-abc2-5e79-900f-14546c13193f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186157332 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-902313f6-5fff-5e8d-b85b-2153357455ee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-902313f6-5fff-5e8d-b85b-2153357455ee" :question/id #uuid "902313f6-5fff-5e8d-b85b-2153357455ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-320766" :question/problem "Write $\\frac{12{x}^{7}}{6{x}^{7}+4}$ in the form $a+\\frac{b}{6{x}^{7}+4},$ where $a\\ne 0.$\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"1\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"30\">$12{x}^{7}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$=$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"25\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"60\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"30\">$6{x}^{7}+4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"25\" width=\"60\">$6{x}^{7}+4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator to put $6{x}^{7}$ in parentheses. Then, we add and subtract $4$ in the parentheses. This reveals a copy of the denominator without changing the value of the expression.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12{x}^{7}}{6{x}^{7}+4} & =\\frac{2(6{x}^{7})}{6{x}^{7}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(6{x}^{7}+4-4)}{6{x}^{7}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2[(6{x}^{7}+4)-(4)]}{6{x}^{7}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(6{x}^{7}+4)-2(4)}{6{x}^{7}+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(6{x}^{7}+4)-8}{6{x}^{7}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we split the fraction into two, and then simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(6{x}^{7}+4)-8}{6{x}^{7}+4} & =\\frac{2(6{x}^{7}+4)}{6{x}^{7}+4}+\\frac{-8}{6{x}^{7}+4} \\\\  & =2+\\frac{-8}{6{x}^{7}+4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24f92d24-8798-5945-aea4-27e7c6675cc0" "answer-field-9b4a5073-566c-54e9-b4bd-3787bd35281f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24f92d24-8798-5945-aea4-27e7c6675cc0" :answer-field/id #uuid "24f92d24-8798-5945-aea4-27e7c6675cc0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-8f9ea0c4-76bf-5905-be8b-b3f2a63ceb17" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8f9ea0c4-76bf-5905-be8b-b3f2a63ceb17"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f9ea0c4-76bf-5905-be8b-b3f2a63ceb17" :answer/id #uuid "8f9ea0c4-76bf-5905-be8b-b3f2a63ceb17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9b4a5073-566c-54e9-b4bd-3787bd35281f" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4a5073-566c-54e9-b4bd-3787bd35281f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-117b0321-12f8-5db2-9373-93df7784178e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-117b0321-12f8-5db2-9373-93df7784178e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-117b0321-12f8-5db2-9373-93df7784178e" :answer/id #uuid "117b0321-12f8-5db2-9373-93df7784178e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-edaa2c54-aa5b-5208-8952-bf397e1fdbf0" :activity/id #uuid "edaa2c54-aa5b-5208-8952-bf397e1fdbf0" :activity/title "Dividing Polynomials by Manipulating Rational Expressions" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049760 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-f1376fc0-9d7b-543a-b10e-d3007a3069f5" "step-4235b559-f92b-5907-83ce-a07cac1ea554" "step-4db876bc-d3bf-597d-a367-4cb3850b1ff5" "step-39388b9c-80f7-5383-a10c-f8f08eb4b7fd" "step-a216f72c-f3f8-5259-aede-da44adc9165c"] :activity/first-step "step-f1376fc0-9d7b-543a-b10e-d3007a3069f5" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-f1376fc0-9d7b-543a-b10e-d3007a3069f5" :step/id #uuid "f1376fc0-9d7b-543a-b10e-d3007a3069f5" :step/content 17592186157915 :step/next "step-4235b559-f92b-5907-83ce-a07cac1ea554" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4235b559-f92b-5907-83ce-a07cac1ea554" :step/id #uuid "4235b559-f92b-5907-83ce-a07cac1ea554" :step/content "question-1f4665bd-3b2f-5e28-98c1-a2915a1c6960" :step/next "step-4db876bc-d3bf-597d-a367-4cb3850b1ff5" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4db876bc-d3bf-597d-a367-4cb3850b1ff5" :step/id #uuid "4db876bc-d3bf-597d-a367-4cb3850b1ff5" :step/content "question-e60ce661-ee8f-513d-978f-4505c3b6113e" :step/next "step-39388b9c-80f7-5383-a10c-f8f08eb4b7fd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-39388b9c-80f7-5383-a10c-f8f08eb4b7fd" :step/id #uuid "39388b9c-80f7-5383-a10c-f8f08eb4b7fd" :step/content "question-2560be5d-dea1-5429-b927-2f169d6e2bc3" :step/next "step-a216f72c-f3f8-5259-aede-da44adc9165c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a216f72c-f3f8-5259-aede-da44adc9165c" :step/id #uuid "a216f72c-f3f8-5259-aede-da44adc9165c" :step/content "question-902313f6-5fff-5e8d-b85b-2153357455ee" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105907 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-443a4021-2ecb-5b8a-948d-b71804528fab" "question-c885246f-c4a6-5da3-b8cb-28ee3dc779d8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-443a4021-2ecb-5b8a-948d-b71804528fab" :question/id #uuid "443a4021-2ecb-5b8a-948d-b71804528fab" :question/math-academy-id "q-280715" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $p=⟨1,0,5⟩$, $q=⟨3,2,6⟩$, and $r=⟨0,4,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-6\\cdot 4)+0+5(3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-22+60 \\\\  & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|38|=38.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2566d49a-718e-5a8c-9b71-cc6e6ef2e3db"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2566d49a-718e-5a8c-9b71-cc6e6ef2e3db" :answer-field/id #uuid "2566d49a-718e-5a8c-9b71-cc6e6ef2e3db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213" :answer/id #uuid "ad103bee-c9bb-538f-b95a-de0c98d63213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "38" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c885246f-c4a6-5da3-b8cb-28ee3dc779d8" :question/id #uuid "c885246f-c4a6-5da3-b8cb-28ee3dc779d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280713" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨2,3,0⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,5⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 2)-3(1\\cdot 6-5\\cdot 0)+0 \\\\  & =2(24-10)-3(6) \\\\  & =28-18 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5ef8f1ee-ea2b-53fa-8813-6530aca61521"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5ef8f1ee-ea2b-53fa-8813-6530aca61521" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ef8f1ee-ea2b-53fa-8813-6530aca61521" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c" :answer/id #uuid "7d46a7ab-4f0b-5721-bebb-a49f4264e23c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105908 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef51444c-d286-591b-9ba9-aedca70d62d8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef51444c-d286-591b-9ba9-aedca70d62d8" :question/id #uuid "ef51444c-d286-591b-9ba9-aedca70d62d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-280746" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,k,2⟩$, $b=⟨1,3,0⟩$, and $c=⟨0,4,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =\\begin{vmatrix}k & k & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{vmatrix}-k\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =k(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)-k(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 0)+2(1\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =k(15)-k(5)+2(4) \\\\  & =15k-5k+8 \\\\  & =10k+8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 10k+8 & =0 \\\\ 10k & =-8 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2170e711-c9bf-56cc-a436-de505690692b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2170e711-c9bf-56cc-a436-de505690692b" :answer-field/id #uuid "2170e711-c9bf-56cc-a436-de505690692b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7" :answer/id #uuid "efac262e-978f-52d8-b514-d218c8e2aaf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105909 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-02e4dd76-291f-501d-9dd9-df687e45b52b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-02e4dd76-291f-501d-9dd9-df687e45b52b" :question/id #uuid "02e4dd76-291f-501d-9dd9-df687e45b52b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280320" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,2,-1),$ $B(3,4,1),$ $C(-1,3,2),$ and $D(2,1,0).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+k)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j+2k)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =-i+j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(2j-k) \\\\  & =2i-j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))-2((-1)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2)+2((-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(1+3)-2(-1-6)+2(1-2) \\\\  & =12-(-14)-2 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|24|=24.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-752eecbd-7383-564b-9c0e-74b4d04c57f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-752eecbd-7383-564b-9c0e-74b4d04c57f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "752eecbd-7383-564b-9c0e-74b4d04c57f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375" :answer/id #uuid "bd4b21f5-ae4e-533c-a49c-e215e4954375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119827 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7e38002f-06be-5b6a-8718-39abfb36add8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7e38002f-06be-5b6a-8718-39abfb36add8" :question/id #uuid "7e38002f-06be-5b6a-8718-39abfb36add8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71022" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-t \\\\ y &=-3-2t \\\\ z &=4+7t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ -3-2t \\\\ 4+7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ -2t \\\\ 7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(0,-3,4)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-1,-2,7⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{-1}=\\frac{y-(-3)}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y+3}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-19df2e81-2346-53c6-b28c-0f1afc312307"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-19df2e81-2346-53c6-b28c-0f1afc312307" :answer-field/id #uuid "19df2e81-2346-53c6-b28c-0f1afc312307" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8ed64ac1-d5c4-5bf3-848a-0de3f90725b2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ed64ac1-d5c4-5bf3-848a-0de3f90725b2" "answer-c75ca808-618d-5710-b5d0-4804627d2e41" "answer-b37bf921-f834-5009-a13c-c6f81e68b8b4" "answer-5dcb7205-b034-5093-9cf9-80e20c097a91" "answer-69cd5697-9cbd-58ff-a0e3-84ea330a8135"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ed64ac1-d5c4-5bf3-848a-0de3f90725b2" :answer/id #uuid "8ed64ac1-d5c4-5bf3-848a-0de3f90725b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y+3}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c75ca808-618d-5710-b5d0-4804627d2e41" :answer/id #uuid "c75ca808-618d-5710-b5d0-4804627d2e41" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y-3}{-2}=\\frac{z+4}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b37bf921-f834-5009-a13c-c6f81e68b8b4" :answer/id #uuid "b37bf921-f834-5009-a13c-c6f81e68b8b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-1}=\\frac{y}{-2}=\\frac{z}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5dcb7205-b034-5093-9cf9-80e20c097a91" :answer/id #uuid "5dcb7205-b034-5093-9cf9-80e20c097a91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{-3}=\\frac{z-7}{4},\\,x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69cd5697-9cbd-58ff-a0e3-84ea330a8135" :answer/id #uuid "69cd5697-9cbd-58ff-a0e3-84ea330a8135" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{-3}=\\frac{z+7}{4},\\,x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119842 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3f6ecd28-8af0-5770-801c-e2211846f047"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3f6ecd28-8af0-5770-801c-e2211846f047" :question/id #uuid "3f6ecd28-8af0-5770-801c-e2211846f047" :question/math-academy-id "q-127457" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{0}=\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{0}=\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-1:$\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2+5t \\\\ 4+7t\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+1}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-1$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=-1\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b7fb6b07-3aa3-5e0b-beb1-701386482c7a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b7fb6b07-3aa3-5e0b-beb1-701386482c7a" :answer-field/id #uuid "b7fb6b07-3aa3-5e0b-beb1-701386482c7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0ce538d-74d3-56e8-9c99-e8c37ca44578" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ecd0c658-006c-55c8-a0a8-ba8100080481" "answer-212fc367-a57d-5039-af89-08026c3e410f" "answer-9050e322-04a0-5d40-9058-40462def8edb" "answer-a0ce538d-74d3-56e8-9c99-e8c37ca44578" "answer-a8ed6ee6-1a77-5ed5-81ec-29a7a1f2a89e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ecd0c658-006c-55c8-a0a8-ba8100080481" :answer/id #uuid "ecd0c658-006c-55c8-a0a8-ba8100080481" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-212fc367-a57d-5039-af89-08026c3e410f" :answer/id #uuid "212fc367-a57d-5039-af89-08026c3e410f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{5}=\\frac{z+4}{7},\\,x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9050e322-04a0-5d40-9058-40462def8edb" :answer/id #uuid "9050e322-04a0-5d40-9058-40462def8edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0ce538d-74d3-56e8-9c99-e8c37ca44578" :answer/id #uuid "a0ce538d-74d3-56e8-9c99-e8c37ca44578" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{5}=\\frac{z-4}{7},\\,x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a8ed6ee6-1a77-5ed5-81ec-29a7a1f2a89e" :answer/id #uuid "a8ed6ee6-1a77-5ed5-81ec-29a7a1f2a89e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{7}=\\frac{z-4}{5},\\,x=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-c9f63623-ba17-5baf-a7ac-b373ec69640a" :activity/id #uuid "c9f63623-ba17-5baf-a7ac-b373ec69640a" :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Line" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186048850 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-72290fe9-7f75-5e81-8a56-0f0853a90f24" "step-be45a931-3267-5e9b-af10-acc0bc85bcf2" "step-40a8a766-a5ff-53c3-a1e8-af197b8d2a13" "step-57929708-6e1f-5624-b944-a9831f7009b2" "step-145ce8df-01ec-57e3-b39c-1ec76660f5ed"] :activity/first-step "step-72290fe9-7f75-5e81-8a56-0f0853a90f24" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-72290fe9-7f75-5e81-8a56-0f0853a90f24" :step/id #uuid "72290fe9-7f75-5e81-8a56-0f0853a90f24" :step/content 17592186120506 :step/next "step-be45a931-3267-5e9b-af10-acc0bc85bcf2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-be45a931-3267-5e9b-af10-acc0bc85bcf2" :step/id #uuid "be45a931-3267-5e9b-af10-acc0bc85bcf2" :step/content "question-7e38002f-06be-5b6a-8718-39abfb36add8" :step/next "step-40a8a766-a5ff-53c3-a1e8-af197b8d2a13" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-40a8a766-a5ff-53c3-a1e8-af197b8d2a13" :step/id #uuid "40a8a766-a5ff-53c3-a1e8-af197b8d2a13" :step/content 17592186338877 :step/next "step-57929708-6e1f-5624-b944-a9831f7009b2" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-57929708-6e1f-5624-b944-a9831f7009b2" :step/id #uuid "57929708-6e1f-5624-b944-a9831f7009b2" :step/content "question-3f6ecd28-8af0-5770-801c-e2211846f047" :step/next "step-145ce8df-01ec-57e3-b39c-1ec76660f5ed" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-145ce8df-01ec-57e3-b39c-1ec76660f5ed" :step/id #uuid "145ce8df-01ec-57e3-b39c-1ec76660f5ed" :step/content 17592186367240 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096620 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17245a50-7006-5425-919f-edc58b5da5cf" "question-e77736b2-0ba9-5e43-b9dd-36b855b6cec7" "question-b512e4a8-0dc7-5d1e-b726-5bdd6894a13e" "question-1cf3cdc5-a966-53dd-81de-da3c76897f3e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-17245a50-7006-5425-919f-edc58b5da5cf" :question/id #uuid "17245a50-7006-5425-919f-edc58b5da5cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-340304" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=1-{x}^{2},$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =1, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})-x\\cdot (-2x)}{{(1-{x}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}}{{(1-{x}^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+{x}^{2}}{{(1-{x}^{2})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b10a7e0-6602-5d46-9e5d-83b14c5c8847"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b10a7e0-6602-5d46-9e5d-83b14c5c8847" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b10a7e0-6602-5d46-9e5d-83b14c5c8847" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5bfe7a9c-764b-5756-917f-0f8851387484" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5bfe7a9c-764b-5756-917f-0f8851387484"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5bfe7a9c-764b-5756-917f-0f8851387484" :answer/id #uuid "5bfe7a9c-764b-5756-917f-0f8851387484" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1+x^2}{(1-x^2)^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e77736b2-0ba9-5e43-b9dd-36b855b6cec7" :question/id #uuid "e77736b2-0ba9-5e43-b9dd-36b855b6cec7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11964" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{9x-7}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=5{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=9x-7,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =10x, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x){v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10x\\cdot (9x-7)-(5{x}^{2})\\cdot 9}{{(9x-7)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{90{x}^{2}-70x-45{x}^{2}}{{(9x-7)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{45{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4323cd0c-0f4d-5d4f-ae6a-7b4d060bf8a5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4323cd0c-0f4d-5d4f-ae6a-7b4d060bf8a5" :answer-field/id #uuid "4323cd0c-0f4d-5d4f-ae6a-7b4d060bf8a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-61ea284d-067f-5b9a-83ae-e4ba28bfec66" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31ec9d49-ec0f-5d76-bc9c-86d2f892bc91" "answer-bb02e585-4b3e-509f-b268-bcda2022d5b1" "answer-33601591-688d-5126-96f4-10f20b0a15f9" "answer-61ea284d-067f-5b9a-83ae-e4ba28bfec66" "answer-428605a0-0dbe-5fff-9ea7-57ac1cd749ca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31ec9d49-ec0f-5d76-bc9c-86d2f892bc91" :answer/id #uuid "31ec9d49-ec0f-5d76-bc9c-86d2f892bc91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{45{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb02e585-4b3e-509f-b268-bcda2022d5b1" :answer/id #uuid "bb02e585-4b3e-509f-b268-bcda2022d5b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{90{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33601591-688d-5126-96f4-10f20b0a15f9" :answer/id #uuid "33601591-688d-5126-96f4-10f20b0a15f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{135{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61ea284d-067f-5b9a-83ae-e4ba28bfec66" :answer/id #uuid "61ea284d-067f-5b9a-83ae-e4ba28bfec66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{45{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-428605a0-0dbe-5fff-9ea7-57ac1cd749ca" :answer/id #uuid "428605a0-0dbe-5fff-9ea7-57ac1cd749ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{90{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b512e4a8-0dc7-5d1e-b726-5bdd6894a13e" :question/id #uuid "b512e4a8-0dc7-5d1e-b726-5bdd6894a13e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340294" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{9x-3}{2x}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=9x-3$ and $v(x)=2x,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =9, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 2x-(9x-3)\\cdot 2}{{(2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18x-18x+6}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-35e9d839-ab63-50d3-994d-eb5f1bec7bef"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-35e9d839-ab63-50d3-994d-eb5f1bec7bef" :answer-field/id #uuid "35e9d839-ab63-50d3-994d-eb5f1bec7bef" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1987e395-8795-5dfc-9572-b75d6b301a14" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1987e395-8795-5dfc-9572-b75d6b301a14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1987e395-8795-5dfc-9572-b75d6b301a14" :answer/id #uuid "1987e395-8795-5dfc-9572-b75d6b301a14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2x^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1cf3cdc5-a966-53dd-81de-da3c76897f3e" :question/id #uuid "1cf3cdc5-a966-53dd-81de-da3c76897f3e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340288" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{-3}{4x-5}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=-3$ and $v(x)=4x-5,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =0, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the quotient rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0\\cdot (4x-5)-(-3)\\cdot 4}{{(4x-5)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{{(4x-5)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c3a7b758-f623-5768-8516-68580ea94477"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c3a7b758-f623-5768-8516-68580ea94477" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3a7b758-f623-5768-8516-68580ea94477" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-67ca8faa-0c3e-513c-8c80-1fdc8856018b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-67ca8faa-0c3e-513c-8c80-1fdc8856018b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-67ca8faa-0c3e-513c-8c80-1fdc8856018b" :answer/id #uuid "67ca8faa-0c3e-513c-8c80-1fdc8856018b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{(4x-5)^2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096621 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-32d1ab28-930b-52ce-95a3-03b4df4fad2a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-32d1ab28-930b-52ce-95a3-03b4df4fad2a" :question/id #uuid "32d1ab28-930b-52ce-95a3-03b4df4fad2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340313" :question/problem "If $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{5}^{x}}$,  find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $v(x)={5}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {5}^{x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot ({5}^{x})^{′}}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot {5}^{x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5)}{{({5}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{{5}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f3ad1214-df3b-5446-bedc-f04cce151e2f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f3ad1214-df3b-5446-bedc-f04cce151e2f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ad1214-df3b-5446-bedc-f04cce151e2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b06ae33d-db5d-59f2-ab18-7eae753b3bbb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b06ae33d-db5d-59f2-ab18-7eae753b3bbb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b06ae33d-db5d-59f2-ab18-7eae753b3bbb" :answer/id #uuid "b06ae33d-db5d-59f2-ab18-7eae753b3bbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\cos x-\\ln(5)\\sin x}{5^x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096622 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-11dd8eeb-96f6-50fa-a820-1e22e1912967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-11dd8eeb-96f6-50fa-a820-1e22e1912967" :question/id #uuid "11dd8eeb-96f6-50fa-a820-1e22e1912967" :question/math-academy-id "q-340339" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{x}},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot ($\n{{field-1}}\n$).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u={x}^{2}$ and $v={2}^{x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}-u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}\\cdot 2x-{x}^{2}\\cdot {2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{({2}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{x}\\cdot x(2-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{{({2}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x(2-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)}{{2}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{2}^{x}}\\cdot (\\,2-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d98c469b-477b-57e5-af28-2ff378fcb14c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d98c469b-477b-57e5-af28-2ff378fcb14c" :answer-field/id #uuid "d98c469b-477b-57e5-af28-2ff378fcb14c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1b8e10fe-6e80-5383-bdd4-03771b7b677d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1b8e10fe-6e80-5383-bdd4-03771b7b677d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b8e10fe-6e80-5383-bdd4-03771b7b677d" :answer/id #uuid "1b8e10fe-6e80-5383-bdd4-03771b7b677d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2-x\\ln 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097820 :tutorial/content "We know how to calculate the derivative of the product of two functions, but what if we have a quotient?\n\nFor that, we can use the **quotient rule**. The quotient rule is a formula to calculate the derivative of the ratio of two functions like \n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac {u(x)}{v(x)}.\n$$\n\nThe quotient rule for differentiation states that the derivative of the function above is given by\n\n$$\nf'(x) = \\dfrac {u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x) \\cdot v'(x)} {[v(x)]^2}.\n$$\n\nFor example, suppose that we have the function $f(x)$ given by\n\n$$\nf(x)= \\dfrac{x}{x^2+1},\n$$\n\nand we want to find $f'(x).$ \n\nHere $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=x^2+1.$  Their derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2}+1)^{′}=2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we plug them in the formula, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)-x\\cdot 2x}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097822 :tutorial/content "We can now prove that $(\\tan x)' = \\sec^2{x}$ using the quotient rule. Here's how! \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{′}}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186096890 :activity/expected-seconds 900.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172028 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-13426e81-09a1-5f21-879b-4654e3684393"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-13426e81-09a1-5f21-879b-4654e3684393" :question/id #uuid "13426e81-09a1-5f21-879b-4654e3684393" :question/math-academy-id "q-95398" :question/problem "Consider the change of variables given by the matrix equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nand the curve $C,$ defined as\n\n$$\nC:\\,{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nGiven that the change of variables above reduces $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ to its canonical (diagonal) form $3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2},$ what type of a quadratic curve is defined by $C?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note the following:\n\n$$\nC:\\,{{{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=2\n$$\n\nLet's write the given change of variables explicitly:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} &=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe know that the given change of variables reduces $Q(x)$ to its canonical form. Therefore, performing the change of variables on $C,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}+2(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2})-2(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}{y}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we complete the square for the variable ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}-2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2} & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}-(\\sqrt{2})^{2}) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-({y}_{2}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}{y}_{2}+2-2) & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{({y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2})}^{2}+2 & =2 \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2}-{({y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2})}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, performing the change of variables\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{z}_{1} &={y}_{1}, \\\\ {z}_{2} &={y}_{2}+\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwe get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}_{1}^{2}-{z}_{2}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis represents the pair of intersecting lines ${z}_{2}=\\sqrt{3}{z}_{1}$ and ${z}_{2}=-\\sqrt{3}{z}_{1}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c1a95532-8eb9-58d2-950f-597816548f39"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1a95532-8eb9-58d2-950f-597816548f39" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1a95532-8eb9-58d2-950f-597816548f39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52c08f07-4189-509a-b220-5216f042453d" "answer-a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" "answer-cd3f94a7-6795-5611-8617-8bdcc199a8ca" "answer-8635fe6e-fac6-55c1-996c-c85b1599c832" "answer-a2d80198-d0f9-5a4a-bda4-ee01da631e00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52c08f07-4189-509a-b220-5216f042453d" :answer/id #uuid "52c08f07-4189-509a-b220-5216f042453d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola with semiaxes $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" :answer/id #uuid "a5629f9b-9362-5ae4-8c5b-612ef5f66982" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A pair of intersecting lines" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd3f94a7-6795-5611-8617-8bdcc199a8ca" :answer/id #uuid "cd3f94a7-6795-5611-8617-8bdcc199a8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8635fe6e-fac6-55c1-996c-c85b1599c832" :answer/id #uuid "8635fe6e-fac6-55c1-996c-c85b1599c832" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An circle of radius $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2d80198-d0f9-5a4a-bda4-ee01da631e00" :answer/id #uuid "a2d80198-d0f9-5a4a-bda4-ee01da631e00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "An ellipse with semiaxes $\\sqrt{3}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172622 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6e371bb6-888d-5045-993d-bc517a769511" :activity/id #uuid "6e371bb6-888d-5045-993d-bc517a769511" :activity/title "Classifying Quadratic Curves" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050760 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-81a51d56-4664-5776-ac0c-6fd45390f9dd" "step-e8039f07-e5ec-5025-bed0-a9260a404806" "step-27f2cabb-08ac-5ca7-a849-181634c81b0c" "step-bdb406eb-4bde-5255-b0ae-21eca3b0a923" "step-fd94ea8f-f9bc-5902-a020-afbc76230738"] :activity/first-step "step-81a51d56-4664-5776-ac0c-6fd45390f9dd" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-81a51d56-4664-5776-ac0c-6fd45390f9dd" :step/id #uuid "81a51d56-4664-5776-ac0c-6fd45390f9dd" :step/content 17592186366629 :step/next "step-e8039f07-e5ec-5025-bed0-a9260a404806" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e8039f07-e5ec-5025-bed0-a9260a404806" :step/id #uuid "e8039f07-e5ec-5025-bed0-a9260a404806" :step/content "question-13426e81-09a1-5f21-879b-4654e3684393" :step/next "step-27f2cabb-08ac-5ca7-a849-181634c81b0c" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-27f2cabb-08ac-5ca7-a849-181634c81b0c" :step/id #uuid "27f2cabb-08ac-5ca7-a849-181634c81b0c" :step/content 17592186172622 :step/next "step-bdb406eb-4bde-5255-b0ae-21eca3b0a923" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bdb406eb-4bde-5255-b0ae-21eca3b0a923" :step/id #uuid "bdb406eb-4bde-5255-b0ae-21eca3b0a923" :step/content 17592186404864 :step/next "step-fd94ea8f-f9bc-5902-a020-afbc76230738" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fd94ea8f-f9bc-5902-a020-afbc76230738" :step/id #uuid "fd94ea8f-f9bc-5902-a020-afbc76230738" :step/content 17592186366732 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-599ba4ee-64d2-5b0c-a2ee-cad2a14843d9" "question-24db3001-b38e-58e0-a2db-d37c5cfbbf6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-599ba4ee-64d2-5b0c-a2ee-cad2a14843d9" :question/id #uuid "599ba4ee-64d2-5b0c-a2ee-cad2a14843d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-29060" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2x-8\\le 4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-8 & \\le 4 \\\\ -2x-8+8 & \\le 4+8 \\\\ -2x+0 & \\le 12 \\\\ -2x & \\le 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,12 \\\\ \\frac{-2x}{-2}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{12}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}x}{\\cancel{-2}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,-6 \\\\ x\\,\\, & \\ge \\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3e6e9bff-56b9-56a9-abf2-3f9a586746de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3e6e9bff-56b9-56a9-abf2-3f9a586746de" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e6e9bff-56b9-56a9-abf2-3f9a586746de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5984d0a1-af5a-506a-bd3d-f4742f93bd1e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c0d8ebb2-e776-553b-bcae-7b8cdfd081ce" "answer-5984d0a1-af5a-506a-bd3d-f4742f93bd1e" "answer-b1bb3fec-7fa5-56c4-bdbc-f9b4538f570f" "answer-ae2737bd-5a02-5f7d-b662-3be2c7a7a4b3" "answer-b8c556c6-37e1-5b77-8d76-57fcbc0b4c3f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0d8ebb2-e776-553b-bcae-7b8cdfd081ce" :answer/id #uuid "c0d8ebb2-e776-553b-bcae-7b8cdfd081ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5984d0a1-af5a-506a-bd3d-f4742f93bd1e" :answer/id #uuid "5984d0a1-af5a-506a-bd3d-f4742f93bd1e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge -6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1bb3fec-7fa5-56c4-bdbc-f9b4538f570f" :answer/id #uuid "b1bb3fec-7fa5-56c4-bdbc-f9b4538f570f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ge 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae2737bd-5a02-5f7d-b662-3be2c7a7a4b3" :answer/id #uuid "ae2737bd-5a02-5f7d-b662-3be2c7a7a4b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8c556c6-37e1-5b77-8d76-57fcbc0b4c3f" :answer/id #uuid "b8c556c6-37e1-5b77-8d76-57fcbc0b4c3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\le -6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-24db3001-b38e-58e0-a2db-d37c5cfbbf6a" :question/id #uuid "24db3001-b38e-58e0-a2db-d37c5cfbbf6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-177678" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $-10x-13<17$ is$\\,x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $13$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x-13 & <17 \\\\ -10x-13+13 & <17+13 \\\\ -10x+0 & <30 \\\\ -10x & <30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-10.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10x\\,\\, & <\\,\\,30 \\\\ \\frac{-10x}{-10}\\, & >\\,\\,\\frac{30}{-10} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-10}x}{\\cancel{-10}}\\, & >\\,\\,-3 \\\\ x\\,\\, & >\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x>-3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d30c22eb-2d07-5424-a15f-025543298f6b" "answer-field-abe5a691-0dde-59ef-aeae-d67842711c04"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d30c22eb-2d07-5424-a15f-025543298f6b" :answer-field/id #uuid "d30c22eb-2d07-5424-a15f-025543298f6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-5a743f62-a91d-5623-8dd4-29eeb4c18ea0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5a743f62-a91d-5623-8dd4-29eeb4c18ea0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a743f62-a91d-5623-8dd4-29eeb4c18ea0" :answer/id #uuid "5a743f62-a91d-5623-8dd4-29eeb4c18ea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-abe5a691-0dde-59ef-aeae-d67842711c04" :answer-field/id #uuid "abe5a691-0dde-59ef-aeae-d67842711c04" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6feeef5c-dcc6-5b6c-99a5-a154469f7a1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6feeef5c-dcc6-5b6c-99a5-a154469f7a1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6feeef5c-dcc6-5b6c-99a5-a154469f7a1d" :answer/id #uuid "6feeef5c-dcc6-5b6c-99a5-a154469f7a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186192844 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-24f35f07-8a41-5d2b-b978-5fe26a8e2dc9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-24f35f07-8a41-5d2b-b978-5fe26a8e2dc9" :question/id #uuid "24f35f07-8a41-5d2b-b978-5fe26a8e2dc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-177686" :question/problem "The solution to the inequality $2<9y-7$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $7$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & <9y-7 \\\\ 2+7 & <9y-7+7 \\\\ 9 & <9y+0 \\\\ 9 & <9y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & <9y \\\\ \\frac{9}{9} & <\\frac{9y}{9} \\\\ 1 & <\\frac{\\cancel{9}y}{\\cancel{9}} \\\\ 1 & <y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\ny>1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y>1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4f06723b-7db7-528a-9b91-ba58a0a4a497" "answer-field-d2881ca4-e313-595d-ad9a-e74eb7ec53fd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4f06723b-7db7-528a-9b91-ba58a0a4a497" :answer-field/id #uuid "4f06723b-7db7-528a-9b91-ba58a0a4a497" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-149864cd-a4f9-5a32-a316-10a25d5c7f51" :answer-field/choices ["answer-149864cd-a4f9-5a32-a316-10a25d5c7f51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-149864cd-a4f9-5a32-a316-10a25d5c7f51" :answer/id #uuid "149864cd-a4f9-5a32-a316-10a25d5c7f51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2881ca4-e313-595d-ad9a-e74eb7ec53fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2881ca4-e313-595d-ad9a-e74eb7ec53fd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1afbb936-56f0-5bfd-83bb-05a7b3ab155f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1afbb936-56f0-5bfd-83bb-05a7b3ab155f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1afbb936-56f0-5bfd-83bb-05a7b3ab155f" :answer/id #uuid "1afbb936-56f0-5bfd-83bb-05a7b3ab155f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-354f1928-0c7c-5c8c-acc7-4c998ed0685b" :activity/id #uuid "354f1928-0c7c-5c8c-acc7-4c998ed0685b" :activity/title "Solving Two-Step Inequalities" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050503 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-5eec0d80-9fb5-59b6-a142-c389b2152a0e" "step-a1244929-29fe-56d1-a501-304c2c5033d4" "step-c9d8eb0d-3333-565c-838b-ead042a6edcd"] :activity/first-step "step-5eec0d80-9fb5-59b6-a142-c389b2152a0e" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-5eec0d80-9fb5-59b6-a142-c389b2152a0e" :step/id #uuid "5eec0d80-9fb5-59b6-a142-c389b2152a0e" :step/content "question-599ba4ee-64d2-5b0c-a2ee-cad2a14843d9" :step/next "step-a1244929-29fe-56d1-a501-304c2c5033d4" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a1244929-29fe-56d1-a501-304c2c5033d4" :step/id #uuid "a1244929-29fe-56d1-a501-304c2c5033d4" :step/content "question-24db3001-b38e-58e0-a2db-d37c5cfbbf6a" :step/next "step-c9d8eb0d-3333-565c-838b-ead042a6edcd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-c9d8eb0d-3333-565c-838b-ead042a6edcd" :step/id #uuid "c9d8eb0d-3333-565c-838b-ead042a6edcd" :step/content "question-24f35f07-8a41-5d2b-b978-5fe26a8e2dc9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119924 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0bcf3acb-d9f4-5535-b8d1-de8e7ee2e9d3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-0bcf3acb-d9f4-5535-b8d1-de8e7ee2e9d3" :question/id #uuid "0bcf3acb-d9f4-5535-b8d1-de8e7ee2e9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-157235" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=0.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3} & =3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6-4-2 \\\\ 9+5-14 \\\\ -3+3+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=3,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-24809e24-c6b5-5bd7-a31f-2f0864640659"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24809e24-c6b5-5bd7-a31f-2f0864640659" :answer-field/id #uuid "24809e24-c6b5-5bd7-a31f-2f0864640659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer-field/choices ["answer-123e6b37-f5d0-58a4-a315-71252699ea45" "answer-49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" "answer-3781813b-d8b2-5b24-921b-dce30178d1ed" "answer-d1f980f5-230b-530c-bbfe-2be36a54ca2f" "answer-7217c7fb-bda2-5564-844d-cd64e72c50f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-123e6b37-f5d0-58a4-a315-71252699ea45" :answer/id #uuid "123e6b37-f5d0-58a4-a315-71252699ea45" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer/id #uuid "49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3781813b-d8b2